      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/dypaca/{size}/2079_2.png",
      "created_at": "2012-10-08T03:26:07.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>I just meant that clearly cards can have effects which are triggered by themselves entering play.&nbsp;&nbsp;So since the Mask of the Matriarch entering play is a non-fowl villain card entering play, it seems like it should go off immediately.</p><p>On the other hand, there are&nbsp;some cards with effects that can only be in effect when they are not in play.&nbsp; I guess it would be fine to say that a card effect cannot be triggered by itself entering play, unless it specifically triggers off of itself entering play...</p>",
